{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_19","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"pwd\ncat > literature_review.md <<'EOF'\n# Literature review: Completion claims on solvable and impossible tasks\n\n## Scope and reading notes (in progress)\nResearch question: Does making a benign task impossible increase unsupported explicit DONE claims for deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Llama-8B? Include executable, state-verifiable tasks, controlled impossibility, and completion-report auditing; exclude pure factual QA and unrelated robotics. Search window: 2023–2026-10-20, with older foundations only as needed. No model outcome is measured during resource gathering.\n\n### ImpossibleBench full reading log\n- Chunk 1, pp. 1–3: Zhong, Raghunathan, Carlini (2025), arXiv:2510.20270v1. One-off mutations contradict a specification; conflicting mutations introduce mutually inconsistent tests. Benchmark success measures exploitation, not whether the final assistant explicitly claims completion. Preserve specification priority and independent checking in our design. Authors report strongly context-dependent exploitation; this does not establish our hypothesized 0.10 effect.\nEOF\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
