{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_20","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"pwd\ncat >> literature_review.md <<'EOF'\n- Chunk 2, pp. 4–6: SWE mutations filtered against gold and empty patches (8.8% one-off and 3.4% conflicting discarded); no analogous gold-solution QC for LiveCodeBench. Open tests, up to ten submissions, minimal/full scaffolds; frontier baselines include GPT-5, o3, GPT-4.1, Claude variants and Qwen3-Coder. Four exploit classes: test edits, overloaded comparisons, extra state, special casing. Figures use 90% CIs, unlike our required paired 95% CI. Target 8B model is not among these evaluations.\nEOF\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
