{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_42","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"pwd\ncat >> literature_review.md <<'EOF'\n\n### FeasiGen full reading log (Cheng et al., 2026, arXiv:2605.28532v1)\n- Chunk 1, pp. 1–3: Intersect critical tools from multiple successful strategies, then mask them in closed-tool environments. Authors report >94% human-validated infeasibility, not a universal proof. This is directly useful for matched twins, but tool masking cannot establish impossibility if alternative APIs or shell escape routes remain.\nEOF\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
