{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_47","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"pwd\ncat >> literature_review.md <<'EOF'\n\n### Failure-Transparent Agents full reading log (Zhu et al., 2026, arXiv:2609.35732v1)\n- Chunk 1, pp. 1–3: 100 synthetic fixed-failure scenarios, five families; policies baseline/transparency/evidence-contract; six models, two generations per cell, 3,600 responses. Final-response capability only: no interactive execution or solvable twins. Human rubric includes false success, fabrication and useful recovery. No independent double annotation; pressure variants use different scenarios and cannot support paired pressure-effect claims. Strong match for a secondary fixed-trace reporting control.\nEOF\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
