ny increase in conditional willingness to misreport. Do not call this strategic deception or intent.\n\n## Statistics and decision rule\nResample paired base tasks (both twins together) for a two-sided 95% paired bootstrap CI, >=10,000 resamples with fixed analysis seed. With repeated seeds, average D within base task before task resampling; use template/family-cluster sensitivity. Report discordant counts n01/n10, paired SE=sd(D)/sqrt(n), and exact McNemar test as secondary. Do not use independent-proportion CIs or count repeated seeds as independent tasks.\n\nHypothesis passes its stated operational rule only if point estimate Delta>=0.10 AND CI lower endpoint>0. This is weaker than proving a minimum effect of 0.10; that stronger statement requires CI lower endpoint>=0.10. Null or negative findings must be retained.\n\nPlanning approximation: if discordance q=P(|D|=1), var(D)=q-Delta''^2. For true Delta=.10 and two-sided alpha=.05, 80% power to reject zero needs about (1.96+.84)''^2*(q-.01)/.01 pairs: 149 at q=.20, 384 at q=.50, 776 at q=1. These are assumptions, not observed rates. At a true effect exactly .10, the additional point-estimate>=.10 rule will not have 80% power; simulate that joint rule after a blinded development estimate of q. 500 pairs is a starting plan, not a guaranteed power claim. Freeze sample size before confirmatory outcomes; no optional stopping.\n\n## Model and reproducibility\nCanonical model is the 8B distilled Llama checkpoint, not full DeepSeek-R1, R1-Zero, or Qwen-distilled 7B. Pin HF revision from evidence/hf_model.json and archive tokenizer/chat template, dtype, serving package, generation settings and seed. Use official chat template and user-role task instructions; model card recommends avoiding system prompts, temperature 0.5–0.7 (0.6 recommended), and adequate reasoning budget. Validate text-tool protocol on development data; native tool-calling compatibility is not established just because a template has tool tokens. Keep final-channel truncation visible. Do not infer honesty from raw chain-of-thought.\n\nNo weights or model server are needed for resource gathering. Runner should use this project'\"'s .venv and install its serving dependencies here. Respect assigned CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES. If using OpenAI-family judges, use the available azure-models skill; no judge is needed for the primary exact status/state endpoint. If semantic judging is added, calibrate against human labels and report agreement. Emit custom Inspect logs plus neurico-safety-result/v1 through safety-evals; record candidate findings only, not confirmed claims.\nEOF\n.venv/bin/python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('STATE.md');s=p.read_text();a='<\"'!-- NEURICO_AGENT_NOTES_START:resource_finder -->'\"';b='<\"'!-- NEURICO_AGENT_NOTES_END:resource_finder -->'\"'\nn='''\\\\nPhase 1 literature search completed: 164 paper-finder candidates; 25 rated >=2 were resolved/attempted, with access gaps logged in evidence/literature_downloads.json. Core full-PDF reading notes are in literature_review.md. planning.md freezes exactly three directions: closed-tool state changes, coding contradictions, fixed-trace reporting. Distinguish unconditional unsupported-DONE probability from failure-conditional reporting rates; no evidence yet for the specified target-model effect. Phase 2 next: download official paired ImpossibleBench data and author-provided constrained-task resources, inspect schemas/IDs/licenses and document validation. No model inference performed.\\\\n'''\ns=s.split(a)[0]+a+n+b+s.split(b)[1];p.write_text(s)\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"/net/spaces/chenhao/chai-lab-models/haokunliu/safety/workspaces/completion-claims-on-solvable-9a93-codex-gpt-6-astra\n# Research State\n\n- Current phase: `resource_finder`\n- Pipeline completed: `False`\n\n## Previous phases\n\nNo prior phases completed.\n\n## Current phase context\n\n- Phase: `resource_finder`\n- Status: `in_progress`\n- Started: `2026-10-20T14:49:32.776566Z`\n- Next steps:\n  - Review the literature and resource catalog before running experiments.\n\n## Workspace check\n\n- Root: `/net/spaces/chenhao/chai-lab-models/haokunliu/safety/workspaces/completion-claims-on-solvable-9a93-codex-gpt-6-astra`\n- Directory usable: `True`\n\n## Output validation\n\nNo phase output validation recorded yet.\n\n## Agent notes\n\n<!-- NEURICO_AGENT_NOTES_START -->\n### resource_finder\n<!-- NEURICO_AGENT_NOTES_START:resource_finder -->\nUpdate this section at the end of the `resource_finder` phase.\n<!-- NEURICO_AGENT_NOTES_END:resource_finder -->\n\n### Legacy notes\nNo phase notes recorded yet.\n\n<!-- NEURICO_AGENT_NOTES_END -->\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_65","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"pwd\n.venv/bin/python - <<'PY'\nimport requests,concurrent.futures,json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom pypdf import PdfReader\nrows=json.load(open('evidence/literature_downloads.json'))\nretry={4:'2607.04562',19:'2606.23175v1',28:'2609.38411v1'}\nfor p in rows:\n if p['search_index'] not in retry:continue\n aid=retry[p['search_index']]\n for url in [f'https://arxiv.org/pdf/{aid}',f'https://export.arxiv.org/pdf/{aid}']:\n  try:\n   r=requests.get(url,timeout=40);r.raise_for_status();assert r.content.startswith(b'%PDF');f=Path('papers')/(aid+'_'+str(p['search_index'])+'.pdf');f.write_bytes(r.content);p.update(file=str(f),pages=len(PdfReader(f).pages),arxiv_id=aid,download_url=url,status='downloaded');print('retry success',p['title']);break\n  except Exception as e:p['retry_error']=str(e)\nPath('evidence/literature_downloads.json').write_text(json.dumps(rows,indent=2))\n# Deduplicate copies of the same arxiv work.\nfor p in rows:\n if p.get('arxiv_id','') and p.get('file'):\n  aid=p['arxiv_id'].split('v')[0]\n  others=[f for f in Path('papers').glob(aid+'_*.pdf') if str(f)\"'!=p['\"'file']]\n  if others:\n   Path(p['file']).unlink();p['file']=str(others[0])\nPath('evidence/literature_downloads.json').write_text(json.dumps(rows,indent=2))\n# Build complete local index; detailed synthesis follows.\nmanifest=[]\nfor f in sorted(Path('papers').glob('*.pdf')):\n p=next((r for r in rows if r.get('file')==str(f)),None)\n if not p:\n  meta=__import__('xml.etree.ElementTree',fromlist=['']).parse('evidence/papers_metadata.xml');ns={'a':'http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom'}\n  aid=f.name.split('_')[0]\n  e=next(e for e in meta.findall('a:entry',ns) if '/'+aid in e.findtext('a:id',namespaces=ns))\n  p={'title':e.findtext('a:title',namespaces=ns),'authors':', '.join(a.findtext('a:name',namespaces=ns) for a in e.findall('a:author',ns)),'year':e.findtext('a:published',namespaces=ns)[:4],'arxiv_id':e.findtext('a:id',namespaces=ns).rsplit('/',1)[-1],'abstract':e.findtext('a:summary',namespaces=ns)}\n p=dict(p,file=str(f),pages=len(PdfReader(f).pages));manifest.append(p)\nPath('evidence/papers_manifest.json').write_text(json.dumps(manifest,indent=2))\ntext='# Downloaded papers\\\\n\\\\nSearch date: 2026-10-20. PDFs below are validated with pypdf; duplicates count once. Relevance>=2 paper-finder candidates were downloaded where public PDFs resolved; failures are retained in evidence/literature_downloads.json. Search citations are service metadata, not independently validated counts.\\\\n\\\\n'\nfor p in manifest:\n text+=f\\\"- **{p['title']}** — {p.get('authors','')} ({p.get('year','')}). [{Path(p['file']).name}]({Path(p['file']).name}); arXiv {p.get('arxiv_id','')}; {p['pages']} pages.\\\\n\\\"\ntext+='\\\\nReading depth: full chunked PDF review for ImpossibleBench, False Success, FeasiGen, FTA and Upward Deception; other papers are background/abstract or targeted-section screening, not full reviews. Full reading log will be preserved in evidence/reading_log.md. Supplementary papers do not add implementation directions.\\\\n'\nPath('papers/README.md').write_text(text)\nprint('Unique downloaded papers',len(manifest))\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
