ccess c(τ, M, H)∈ {0,1}also depends on the agent. Thus a feasible ta\n1f= 0 b= 1 Proceed✓ Proceed× b= 0 Defer× Defer✓ Let t⋆ denote the first point at which decisive feasibility evidence is available, possibly af- ter a tool call. Write bt⋆ (τ)∈[0,1] for the agent’s separately elicited feasibility belief and at⋆ (τ)∈ {commit,defer} for its observed meta-action. The task-defined warranted action is a⋆(τ) = \u001acommit, f(τ) = 1, defer, f(τ) \nfeasigen\nimpossiblebench\nupward-deception\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
