ction caveat: \"'`build_path_dataset.py` accepts `task_success=None` traces with nonempty tool_call_set as successful. Tighten to verified success for our task construction. Set min-agreement=1.0 and still audit alternate solution paths; observed tool-set intersection is not proof of indispensability.\n- Upstream scripts default output under `code/feasigen/data/`; adapt output paths to this workspace'\"'s datasets/ and evidence/ before executing. No source-download, inference, model server or paid API run was started.\n\n## Reclone at recorded commits\n\n\"'```bash\npwd\ngit clone --depth 1 https://github.com/safety-research/impossiblebench.git code/impossiblebench\ngit clone --depth 1 https://github.com/QingyuLiu/Agentic-Upward-Deception.git code/upward-deception\ngit clone --depth 1 https://github.com/LeonChengg/FeasiGen.git code/feasigen\n```\n\nFor future reproduction fetch the SHA in `evidence/repositories.json` and checkout that SHA; a default-branch shallow clone alone is not a pin. Existing clones already match these SHAs. Do not rerun clone commands over existing directories.\nEOF\ncat > code/.gitignore <<'\"'EOF'\n/*/\nEOF\n.venv/bin/python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('STATE.md');s=p.read_text();a='<\"'!-- NEURICO_AGENT_NOTES_START:resource_finder -->'\"';b='<\"'!-- NEURICO_AGENT_NOTES_END:resource_finder -->'\"'\nn='''\\\\nPhases 1–3 complete: 26 unique PDFs; two official datasets (103 x 3 LCB rows; 200 Upward Deception tasks), 30 synthetic development-only pairs; three official repos cloned/pinned. planning.md keeps exactly three directions. Evidence: papers_manifest.json, dataset_validation.json, development_validation.json, repositories.json, code_validation.json under evidence/. code/README.md documents runtime dependencies and scorer caveats; 60 Python files parse, no evaluation runtime claimed. Known data defects: lcbhard_77 syntax errors; 48 altered-word prompts. FeasiGen lacks released task data and accepts some unverified-success traces. Primary endpoint must use independent state and final DONE parsing, not upstream exploitation/HFR scores. Phase 4 next: concise literature synthesis, complete resource catalog, final artifact/hash audit; no model hypothesis result.\\\\n'''\np.write_text(s.split(a)[0]+a+n+b+s.split(b)[1])\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"/net/spaces/chenhao/chai-lab-models/haokunliu/safety/workspaces/completion-claims-on-solvable-9a93-codex-gpt-6-astra\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_84","type":"agent_message","text":"The three official repositories are pinned and inspected. Their scorers measure different outcomes, so the handoff identifies what can be reused and where the runner needs separate DONE and state checks. I’m consolidating the literature notes and resource catalog, then auditing files, hashes, exclusions, and outstanding jobs before creating the completion marker.\n"}}
